The probability density function (PDF) must integrate to 1 over its entire domain.
The function is $f(x) = K e^{-|x|}$ for $|x| < 4$ (i.e., $-4 < x < 4$) and 0 otherwise.
$$ \int_{-\infty}^{\infty} f(x) dx = 1 $$
$$ \int_{-4}^{4} K e^{-|x|} dx = 1 $$
Since $e^{-|x|}$ is an even function, we can integrate from 0 to 4 and multiply by 2:
$$ 2K \int_{0}^{4} e^{-x} dx = 1 $$
$$ 2K \left[ -e^{-x} \right]_{0}^{4} = 1 $$
$$ 2K (-e^{-4} - (-e^{0})) = 1 $$
$$ 2K (1 - e^{-4}) = 1 $$
$$ K = \frac{1}{2(1 - e^{-4})} $$
